# Parallel tool calls in a single assistant turn. We ask for two
# independent bash commands and assert that BOTH stdout strings appear
# on the grid. Whether the provider actually parallelises the calls or
# serialises them is an implementation detail of the model. What we
# care about: zag has to register two distinct tool_use blocks and
# wire two tool_result events back in. A regression in tool_use id
# correlation or tool_result ordering would drop one of these.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "In a SINGLE assistant turn, issue two bash tool calls in parallel: one running 'echo zag-par-A-K8' and one running 'echo zag-par-B-Y5'. Do not print the tokens any other way." <Enter>
wait_idle 40s
expect_text /zag-par-A-K8/
expect_text /zag-par-B-Y5/
snapshot final
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
